From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: --save-and-quit: output filename, exit status, no dialogs

Make --save-and-quit usable from scripts:

 - --save-and-quit=FILE saves to FILE instead of diff.pdf.
 - Exit with status 0 if the files appear the same, 1 if they differ,
   and 2 on trouble, as diff(1) does.  Nothing is written if the files
   appear the same.
 - Do not show the main window, and report errors on stderr rather than
   in modal message boxes, which would block an unattended run.
 - Check that the output file can be written before rendering into it.
 - Fix comparing two files given on the command line in batch mode: both
   filename fields start out filled in, so setFile1() saw the second
   file there.
 - Document the options and exit status in the man page.

Forwarded: no
---
--- a/diffpdf.1.cmake
+++ b/diffpdf.1.cmake
@@ -26,6 +26,27 @@ second. This will make DiffPDF compare p
 If the program is passed two PDF filenames on the command line it will
 start up and compare those files in Text mode (or in Appearance mode if
 the filenames are preceded by \-a or \-\-appearance).
+.SH OPTIONS
+.TP
+.BR \-a ", " \-\-appearance ", " \-c ", " \-\-characters ", " \-w ", " \-\-words
+Set the initial comparison mode.
+.TP
+.BR \-\-save\-and\-quit [ =\fIfile.pdf\fP ]
+Compare the two files given without showing a window.  If they differ,
+save the differing pages, with the differences highlighted, to
+.I file.pdf
+(default
+.IR diff.pdf ),
+replacing any existing file.  If they appear to be the same, no file
+is written.
+.TP
+.B \-\-help
+Show all options.
+.SH "EXIT STATUS"
+With
+.BR \-\-save\-and\-quit ,
+the exit status is 0 if the files appear to be the same, 1 if they
+differ, and 2 if there was trouble (e.g., a file could not be read).
 .SH FILES
 .TP
 .I ~/.config/DiffPDF/DiffPDF.conf
